Backport of two upstream cocotb fixes onto v2.0.1 (both master-only as of
2026-08-04, latest release v2.0.1):

* cocotb/cocotb#5423 (commit 709a75c99f74fa2fef948cd6325e63a854bf97ec):
  "Resolved Verilator hanging when st:fatal is triggered in waves enabled
  simulations". wrap_up() runs as a Verilated exit callback; deleting the
  trace object there re-enters Verilated::removeExitCb(), which relocks the
  s_exitMutex that runExitCallbacks() is still holding -> self-deadlock.
  Any $stop/$error/$fatal (e.g. an RTL assertion under --assert) with
  --trace/--trace-fst then hangs the simulation process forever at 100% CPU
  instead of exiting. Close the trace in the callback, delete it on the
  normal main() exit path.

* cocotb/cocotb commit 555b88f3b91bb031bf090aa2c2b816c34a8fc575:
  "[Verilator] Updated verilator to exit with non-zero status code if any
  asserts were triggered". Without this, a $error that does not $stop would
  end the sim with exit code 0.

Drop this patch when the flake's nixpkgs pin ships a cocotb release
containing both commits (> 2.0.1).

--- a/src/cocotb/share/lib/verilator/verilator.cpp
+++ b/src/cocotb/share/lib/verilator/verilator.cpp
@@ -58,8 +58,8 @@
 
 #if VM_TRACE
     if (tfp) {
-        delete tfp;
-        tfp = nullptr;
+        // We don't delete the trace object to avoid deadlock in verilator sims.
+        tfp->close();
     }
 #endif
 
@@ -205,5 +205,17 @@
 
     wrap_up();
 
+#if VM_TRACE
+    if (tfp) {
+        delete tfp;
+        tfp = nullptr;
+    }
+#endif
+
+    // Fail the sim if any assertion/error fired during the run.
+    if (Verilated::threadContextp()->errorCount() > 0) {
+        return 1;
+    }
+
     return 0;
 }
